<p>Nepal votes on March 5 in a high-stakes election shaped by last year’s youth-led protests, driven by anger over corruption, unemployment and entrenched political elites. Established parties are once again battling for power, even as newer or non-traditional figures run on promises of cleaner governance and a break from familiar political patterns. Several reports highlight the election’s emotional weight for young Nepalis who were injured in the unrest or lost loved ones—reminders of the uprising’s cost, and of the hope that voting can bring accountability and practical change. With a large youth population, the vote is widely seen as a test of whether Gen Z will turn street protest energy into electoral choices—and whether the political class will respond to those demands.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/KNOGNz61HtbbcjVwKxwnQc4c-K0PZz2H6Xdgv2t7M7hhJsbtORD-AiNPnXpid91erqPMlOQKchvKqH5qopkZ3YIe_JfKaTrE6ZcX8wV5cgaje_WOPHIt4gr-2bktdn3LO5_FGJL-iToVU3dqdQSlFa15xApQxyBcZzQKTAPzQVX_Q0BLFsj8' alt='Voters and campaign activity ahead of Nepal’s March 5 election.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Youth demographics: About 46% of Nepal’s population is under 24, putting younger voters at the center of the election outcome.</li><li>Violence legacy: Last year’s Kathmandu unrest killed at least 77 people, a toll that continues to shape youth expectations of accountability.</li><li>New challenger: Balendra Shah (“Balen”), a 35-year-old rapper-turned-politician who won Kathmandu’s mayoral race in May 2022, has become a leading symbol of anti-establishment politics heading into the vote.</li><li>Political fallout: The Hindu says the March 5 vote follows youth-led protests that toppled the CPN-UML government led by K.P. Sharma Oli, which had been backed by the Nepali Congress.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>One protest survivor: Sangharsh Bhusal returned to the spot outside Nepal’s parliament building where police shot him during last year’s violence, and he says candidates should avoid “the same old patterns”. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/week-asia/politics/article/3345168/young-nepalis-hope-post-uprising-election-candidates-shun-same-old-patterns'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Gen Z activists and voters: Reports describe deep disenchantment with established parties after last year’s protests, along with uncertainty over whether young voters will still back those same parties at the ballot box. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/3/nepals-gen-z-threw-out-old-parties-will-it-vote-for-them-in-key-election'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Anti-establishment campaigners: Coverage of Balendra Shah frames his appeal as rooted in pop-culture visibility and sharp criticism of the ruling elite, setting him up against a veteran political heavyweight in Damak. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/03/nepal-gen-z-election-popular-former-rapper-balen'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Established parties: The Hindu frames the contest as old parties trying to hang on to influence after the youth-led protests that brought down K.P. Sharma Oli’s CPN-UML-led government, while newer groups pitch themselves as vehicles for change. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/old-parties-dig-in-new-ones-offer-change-as-nepal-heads-to-the-polls/article70695936.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/old-parties-dig-in-new-ones-offer-change-as-nepal-heads-to-the-polls/article70695936.ece'>Old parties dig in, new ones offer change as Nepal heads to the polls</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/3/nepals-gen-z-threw-out-old-parties-will-it-vote-for-them-in-key-election'>Nepal’s Gen Z threw out old parties. Will it vote for them in key election?</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/nepals-gen-z-uprising-took-their-loved-ones-now-they-hope-for-change-11161190#publisher=newsstand'>Nepal&#x27;s Gen-Z Uprising Took Their Loved Ones. Now They Hope For Change</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/week-asia/politics/article/3345168/young-nepalis-hope-post-uprising-election-candidates-shun-same-old-patterns'>Young Nepalis hope post-uprising election candidates shun ‘same old patterns’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/03/nepal-gen-z-election-popular-former-rapper-balen'>Nepal’s gen-Z election: can popular former rapper Balen topple a veteran political heavyweight?</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>